  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <div class="panel active" id="overview">
    <div class="week-note">
      <b>How this works.</b> Every week has the same shape. Sunday you cook <b>Batch A</b> — one protein, one carb, one or two vegetables — enough for Sunday dinner through Tuesday. Wednesday you cook <b>Batch B</b> the same way, covering Wednesday dinner through Friday. Saturday is a flex day: leftovers, a quick pantry meal, or eating out. Breakfast is your sweet potato + eggs by default, with oats or a smoothie swapped in a couple of times a week. This keeps each prep day to one protein + one pot of carbs + a tray of vegetables — not eight separate dishes.
    </div>
    <div class="grid2">
      <div class="snack"><h4>Iron</h4><p>You're already supplementing iron — the liver, beef, beans and chickpeas through this plan are food-level support on top of that, always paired with a vitamin-C food to help absorption. See Nutrition Notes.</p></div>
      <div class="snack"><h4>Vitamin D</h4><p>You're already supplementing vitamin D too. Salmon, tilapia and eggs are worked in through most weeks as food-level backup on top of the supplement.</p></div>
      <div class="snack"><h4>Cholesterol</h4><p>Liver appears once, in a small blended portion. Fish and plant protein (tofu, chickpeas, beans) cover 5 of the 8 batches. Oats, chia and beans bring the soluble fibre that helps manage LDL.</p></div>
      <div class="snack"><h4>Muscle</h4><p>Every lunch and dinner is built around a full protein portion plus a starchy carb, with a slight calorie surplus in mind for 3–4 training days a week.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

